## contact-forces

contact-forces-ask = Which forces act without touching?
contact-forces-title = Contact and non-contact forces
contact-forces-question = Bodies act on each other — but do they always have to touch? Six observations, all with numbers: a steel ball over a magnet on scales, { $gap } apart, the same through a card, a rubbed comb over bits of paper, a block on the table, the same block above the table, and a { $mass } weight on a dynamometer, let go. Which forces act without touching?
contact-forces-choices = Magnetic, electric and gravity; friction and elasticity — only when touching
contact-forces-choices-2 = None: forces pass only by touching (through the air at least)
contact-forces-choices-3 = Only the magnetic one
contact-forces-setup = Electronic scales, a stand, a steel ball on a thread, a bar magnet, a card, a plastic comb, bits of paper, a block, a dynamometer, weights
contact-forces-gap = Gap between the magnet and the ball
contact-forces-magnet-label = Magnet
contact-forces-magnet-ferrite = Ferrite
contact-forces-magnet-neodymium = Neodymium (N35)
contact-forces-mass = Mass of the weight
